{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "03207",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.28,
      "end_seconds": 7.65,
      "duration_seconds": 6.37,
      "text": "hello doctor, sorry, I took a wrong turn on the way here"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 9.0,
      "end_seconds": 12.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.85,
      "text": "Come in. Please sit. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 14.31,
      "end_seconds": 29.55,
      "duration_seconds": 15.24,
      "text": "Doctor, um, it's a sudden severe tummy pain. It's getting on my nerves now. A neighbour of mine said I should see someone about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 31.07,
      "end_seconds": 39.77,
      "duration_seconds": 8.7,
      "text": "Okay, so the the vitals from earlier. Pressure 126 over 70, oxygen saturation is 97 percent. Temperature 36.7, pulse 125."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 40.81,
      "end_seconds": 41.84,
      "duration_seconds": 1.03,
      "text": "Okay, noted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 58.95,
      "end_seconds": 61.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.12,
      "text": "Okay, when did this begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 62.9,
      "end_seconds": 72.49,
      "duration_seconds": 9.59,
      "text": "So, it's been going on for about a week. I'm not great at remembering details, so bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 72.72,
      "end_seconds": 75.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "Mm-hmm. Does anything help it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 78.68,
      "end_seconds": 94.72,
      "duration_seconds": 16.04,
      "text": "Only lying still, and it's not much. I've, I've had shoulder tip pain too, for two months. Oh, and pain spreading all over. That's been about the same, five days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 95.86,
      "end_seconds": 100.55,
      "duration_seconds": 4.69,
      "text": "and what about blood in the vomit, diarrhoea or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 102.19,
      "end_seconds": 104.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.53,
      "text": "Nope, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 105.52,
      "end_seconds": 108.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "Any breathing difficulties apart from this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 109.73,
      "end_seconds": 111.58,
      "duration_seconds": 1.85,
      "text": "No, nothing there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 112.39,
      "end_seconds": 114.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "Any rashes or skin problems otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 115.88,
      "end_seconds": 118.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "No, skin's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 122.97,
      "end_seconds": 125.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "now some background about your lifestyle"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 127.83,
      "end_seconds": 140.12,
      "duration_seconds": 12.29,
      "text": "I'm vegetarian and have been for years. No, I share a house with my brother. I do a yoga class on Thursdays."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.47,
      "end_seconds": 145.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "which medicines do you take at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 147.02,
      "end_seconds": 151.59,
      "duration_seconds": 4.57,
      "text": "I take alendronate, 70 milligrams, once a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 152.59,
      "end_seconds": 154.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "When did you start it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 156.79,
      "end_seconds": 159.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "for about a year"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.15,
      "end_seconds": 163.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "let me ask about allergies, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.07,
      "end_seconds": 168.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.1,
      "text": "Not to my knowledge, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 180.37,
      "end_seconds": 183.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "has anyone ever diagnosed you with something?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 184.42,
      "end_seconds": 189.53,
      "duration_seconds": 5.11,
      "text": "Erm, I've had thin bones for nearly five years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 190.77,
      "end_seconds": 195.94,
      "duration_seconds": 5.17,
      "text": "I'll need to examine you for this, it won't take long."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 197.29,
      "end_seconds": 198.46,
      "duration_seconds": 1.17,
      "text": "Look straight ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.77,
      "end_seconds": 220.39,
      "duration_seconds": 7.62,
      "text": "your tummy is rigid like a board and very tender everywhere, and you are lying completely still"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 223.98,
      "end_seconds": 235.36,
      "duration_seconds": 11.38,
      "text": "Okay, that's enough for me. Right, here's what I'm thinking. I don't have a clear answer today: a perforated stomach ulcer is possible, and so is pancreatitis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 252.11,
      "end_seconds": 271.04,
      "duration_seconds": 18.93,
      "text": "let's book an erect chest X-ray to look into possible perforation i'll request a CT scan, it'll help with possible perforation the result will help us decide whether anything more is needed nothing to eat or drink, you need an operation urgently"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 271.61,
      "end_seconds": 299.21,
      "duration_seconds": 27.6,
      "text": "Okay, go on. I'll also refer you to the surgical team. If it hasn't settled next month, we'd think about urgent blood tests, but not now. Keep an eye out, and if the symptoms get worse, call us the same day or go to emergency. See me again straight away. Let me check I've been clear. What will you do once you get home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 300.15,
      "end_seconds": 305.68,
      "duration_seconds": 5.53,
      "text": "so, I come back straight away is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 306.61,
      "end_seconds": 311.69,
      "duration_seconds": 5.08,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Anything else on your mind before you go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 313.18,
      "end_seconds": 316.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.62,
      "text": "No, that's all. Thanks a lot."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 318.82,
      "end_seconds": 320.22,
      "duration_seconds": 1.4,
      "text": "Look after yourself."
    }
  ]
}